WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.850
The intertwined fates of men

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:04.710
give the Mononoke its Form,

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:10.780
And so, I’ll ask you all to tell me

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:15.200
the Truth and Regret!

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:44.730
<b>Yo, yo, yonaka ni bakko suru chimi mouryou</b>

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:44.730
<i>Yo, yo, at midnight evil spirits stalk</i>

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:46.820
<b>Marude ikaino ichimi routou</b>

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:46.820
<i>As if they're from another world</i>

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:49.070
<b>Mitai na rhymer rhyme shini toujou</b>

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:49.070
<i>Come to rhyme rhymes</i>

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.240
<b>Kikoetarou? Yamini hibiku oto</b>

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.240
<i>Can you hear them? The sounds resonating from the darkness</i>

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:53.580
<b>Bibitte kyomi nai furi shiyouto</b>

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:53.580
<i>Scared senseless, but you pretend not to be interested</i>

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:55.540
<b>Koukishin wa hini hini jyoushou</b>

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:55.540
<i>Your curiosity grows day by day</i>

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:57.830
<b>Nara check shini ikou, here we, here we go ya'll!</b>

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:57.830
<i>So let's go check them out, here we, here we go ya'll</i>

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:00.040
<b>Ayashi ayaushi shima no chimi mouryou</b>

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:00.040
<i>The mysterious and dangerous evil spirits</i>

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:01.710
<b>Tabun jigoku wa manpai</b>

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:01.710
<i>Hell is probably full with evil spirits</i>

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:05.000
<b>Afure dashita renchuu ga dantai de retsu wo nashite</b>

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:05.000
<i>Those that can't get in march in a line</i>

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:06.210
<b>Kono yo ni stand-by</b>

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:06.210
<i>Waiting on stand-by in this world</i>

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.420
<b>Yatsura no bun basho ga mazu tannai</b>

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.420
<i>There aren't any spaces left for them</i>

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:10.630
<b>Dooride kisetsu towazu atsui hazu</b>

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:10.630
<i>No wonder, no matter what the season is, it's always hot</i>

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:13.300
<b>Aete heat up sasu ikatsui verse wo</b>

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:13.300
<i>Purposely heating you up with hot verses</i>

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:14.970
<b>Kamashite ase kakasuzo</b>

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:14.970
<i>That make you sweat</i>

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:17.770
<b>Douse yakedaro kikasena gasshou wo yo!</b>

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:17.770
<i>You might as well let us hear you all sing!</i>

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:19.810
<b>HA! Koitsuwa marude kajiba</b>

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:19.810
<i>HA! It's just like a scene of a fire</i>

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:22.230
<b>Sugee nekki tamacchimau shimaguni</b>

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:22.230
<i>The excitement in the air heats up this island country</i>

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:24.360
<b>DANGER! Masu masu agacchimau COME ON!</b>

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:24.360
<i>DANGER! The tension keeps building COME ON!</i>

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.610
<b>(Kono Jipangu mouchoi de panku!)</b>

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.610
<i>(This Japan is about to explode!)</i>

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:28.740
<b>HA! Koitsuwa marude kajiba</b>

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:28.740
<i>HA! It's just like a scene of a fire</i>

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:31.030
<b>Sugee nekki tamacchimau shimaguni</b>

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:31.030
<i>The excitement in the air heats up this island country</i>

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:33.240
<b>DANGER! Masu masu agacchimau COME ON!</b>

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:33.240
<i>DANGER! The tension keeps building COME ON!</i>

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:35.450
<b>(Kono Jipangu mouchoi de panku!)</b>

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:35.450
<i>(This Japan is about to explode!)</i>

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:38.450
<b><i>Act Two</i></b>

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:08.510
Hey, I’m out of sake.

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:10.970
Someone get me some more.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:15.950
Sato…

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:17.230
Right away!

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:18.780
Kayo, go get it.

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:21.750
Hurry, fetch the good sake.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:23.450
You know where we keep it.

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:25.960
I-I don’t want to…

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:27.450
What do you mean?!

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:29.780
You were the one he asked!

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:31.430
I don’t want to leave this room!

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:33.460
How dare you talk back to me!

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:35.490
Hey! Where do you think you’re going?

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.840
I need some salt.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:39.940
I might as well get the sake, too.

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:41.640
Don’t move unless I tell you to!

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:44.180
It will come for us again.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:46.050
I need to be ready for it.

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:47.650
No way! Stay put!

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:49.760
You haven’t earned my trust yet.

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:51.920
Then why don’t you come along with me?

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:54.390
I’d appreciate it if you did, actually.

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:55.790
Sure! I’ll go!

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:59.350
I’m sorry for foiling your one
and only opportunity to escape!

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:02.490
I’m opening it.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:09.610
I sure am lucky, having a bodyguard.

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:10.900
I’ll go as well!

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:20.980
Now, then…

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:22.280
Shall we get going?

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:26.450
You’re heading to the kitchen?

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:27.790
I just need some salt.

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:28.850
Yeah, right.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:31.660
He’s going to try and poison us!

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:33.490
He’s not like that.

00:03:33.490 --> 00:03:36.050
Why do you have to talk about him like that?

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:39.190
Well, uh…

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:43.770
Where is it?

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:45.070
I’ll go get it.

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:46.830
We keep it behind the stove.

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:50.270
Wait right there.

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:52.410
You won’t leave or anything, right?

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:54.210
I won’t move!

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:55.370
Don’t you worry!

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:06.090
Ow! Who spilled oil over here?

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:08.880
It’s usually stored some place out of the way.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:11.060
Inexcusable! Who could have done this?

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:20.300
Hey! You expect me to carry this?!

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:23.140
To make sure I don’t
have a chance to poison it.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:26.780
You overheard me?

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:28.810
You talk so loud,

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:30.920
it’d be impossible not to hear you.

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:32.450
You’re making fun of me!

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:34.700
Uh-oh. You noticed.

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:35.870
Hold it!

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:37.150
Where are you going?!

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:39.620
I said we need to be ready.

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:44.630
I brought some sake.

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:45.830
What is that?

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:47.800
You’ve never seen salt?

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:49.510
I know it’s salt!

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:51.890
I’m asking you what it’s for!

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.830
I thought you’d do
something more fancy with it.

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:00.140
What the hell is this?

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:05.750
You can make fun of it all you want.

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:06.740
However,

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:09.150
don’t break the line.

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:11.760
Line? Of salt?

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:12.740
Exactly.

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:16.120
It’s all just superstition.
Don’t make a big deal about it.

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:18.370
If that’s what you think, that’s fine.

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:21.040
But do not step into the enclosure of salt.

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:23.600
For any reason.

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:30.040
Umm, is there anything I can help with?

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:31.540
Actually, there is.

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:36.280
You are much more dependable
than this half-wit big mouth.

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:38.020
Who are you calling a half-wit?!

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:39.380
Hold this.

00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:43.620
Hand me what’s in the
box, one thing at a time.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:44.590
All right!

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:49.110
What’s that contraption?

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:50.700
Never seen a scale?

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:52.160
A scale?

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:53.390
Hold out your finger.

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:56.430
It’s okay.

00:05:56.430 --> 00:05:57.660
Just like that.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:05.340
I think it likes you, Kayo.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:07.240
Lift your finger up a little.

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:26.230
Keep doing that.

00:06:26.230 --> 00:06:27.770
Okay!

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:29.810
What are you measuring with this?

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:31.480
The weight of the Mononoke?

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:32.540
Distance.

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:33.740
Distance?

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:36.030
To measure the distance to the Mononoke.

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:38.320
Don’t you know what scales are for?

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:41.080
They aren’t for measuring distance,

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:42.540
they’re for weight!

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:46.830
Hey!

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:48.000
Are you listening?

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:53.420
You said you were going
to get rid of the Mononoke.

00:06:54.670 --> 00:06:55.550
Yeah.

00:06:55.550 --> 00:06:59.300
Then we shouldn’t be
wasting our time like this!

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:01.680
Hurry up and kill that evil beast!

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:04.560
If you can’t do it,
then you’ve been lying all along!

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:09.200
I’m sure I told you.

00:07:10.210 --> 00:07:11.880
To destroy the Mononoke,

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:14.980
we still need its Truth and Regret.

00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:18.750
Until those become clear,
the sword can’t be unsheathed.

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:29.620
The intertwined fates of men

00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:31.130
give the Mononoke its Form,

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:34.290
I want to know the Truth and Regret.

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:38.600
So, what is this Truth
and Regret you talk about?

00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:40.930
And why should we talk about them?

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:43.140
Truth is the basic facts.

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:45.260
Regret is the motive behind its grudge.

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:46.600
So, what about it?

00:07:46.600 --> 00:07:49.770
Something happened
and for whatever reason,

00:07:49.770 --> 00:07:51.150
the spirit bears a grudge.

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:53.050
Unless everything becomes clear,

00:07:53.050 --> 00:07:57.420
the sword will hold no power and
cannot cut down the Mononoke.

00:07:57.420 --> 00:07:59.400
The reason behind it, huh?

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:02.820
Firstly,

00:08:02.820 --> 00:08:07.080
why are there no cats in this house?

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:09.750
Someone must have done something to a cat.

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:11.750
What could it have been?

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:14.840
A cat’s grudge can haunt humans?

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:19.050
You think a lowly beast
is capable of such an extreme act?

00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:21.430
I wouldn’t know.

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:24.100
But there’s definitely a Mononoke.

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:25.760
But, a grudge?

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:28.720
I mean, they kept coming into the kitchen,

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:31.350
so I’d splash water or chase them out.

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:34.360
But they wouldn’t hold
grudges or haunt us for that?

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:35.520
There’s no way!

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:36.570
It’s possible.

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:37.940
Why?

00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:39.860
It’s not that serious.

00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:42.910
Mononoke have their own reasoning.

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:46.950
Their grudges can sometimes
never be explained or understood.

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:49.580
Like a big misunderstanding,

00:08:49.580 --> 00:08:53.750
the grudge may not
require any logic or coherence.

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:55.540
No way…

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:59.510
Other people have done stuff
a lot worse than what I did!

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:01.170
W-What do you mean?

00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:03.090
I know about it!

00:09:03.090 --> 00:09:05.010
Ms. Sato has been buying cats.

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:06.020
Buying cats?

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:08.760
All I did was pay for them and nothing more.

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:10.530
And? What happened to them?

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:13.460
I don’t know what became of those cats.

00:09:13.460 --> 00:09:15.440
It was all Yahei’s doing.

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:17.560
Whose money was it?

00:09:19.270 --> 00:09:22.530
You don’t have to answer…

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:24.840
It was Sasaoka’s!

00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:27.810
Sasaoka told me to buy the cats,

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:31.080
and Yahei took them away. That’s all I know.

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:33.520
Actually… Well…

00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:35.250
We slayed them.

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:39.920
Isn’t that right? I think about twenty of them.

00:09:39.920 --> 00:09:43.050
We got some good imitation Kotetsu katanas.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:41.340
How could you…?!

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:45.840
Even though they were fake,
the blades were good quality.

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:48.400
The fur of a cat is very soft.

00:09:48.390 --> 00:09:52.020
The bones are delicate, but the hide is thick.

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:55.020
It’s perfect for testing a sword.

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:57.580
Right, Sasaoka?

00:09:57.580 --> 00:09:59.140
Indeed.

00:09:59.150 --> 00:10:01.110
Forgive my impudence Master Yoshikuni…

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:03.990
…but don’t you feel that’s somewhat unjust?

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:05.200
Sasaoka,

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:07.160
why didn’t you prevent this?

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:09.200
Remonstrance is part of a vassal’s duty!

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:10.990
So we should have killed dogs instead?

00:10:10.990 --> 00:10:12.660
That’s not what I’m implying!

00:10:12.660 --> 00:10:16.630
It’s proper to suggest an
alternative if you criticize a decision.

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:19.960
You’ve just demonstrated
your discontent, Katsuyama.

00:10:19.960 --> 00:10:21.900
Discontent?!

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:23.300
More importantly,

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:24.800
didn’t you recommend Yoshiaki

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:27.970
over Yoshikuni as the successor to the house?

00:10:27.970 --> 00:10:33.020
How do you plan to take
responsibility for our situation?

00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:36.610
How can you keep such a straight
face in these grave circumstances?

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:39.320
I don’t work under you, Katsuyama.

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:41.920
So you’ve revealed
your true intentions, Sasaoka!

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:43.820
Enough of this!

00:10:43.820 --> 00:10:46.090
This is hardly the time!

00:10:46.090 --> 00:10:48.160
But elder master…

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:50.020
Silence, Sasaoka.

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:54.500
Now, both of you…

00:10:54.500 --> 00:11:00.920
Stop your quarrelling and
focus on what we should do.

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:04.050
Mao, who agreed to
sacrifice herself for our clan,

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:06.170
is lying here in this state.

00:11:06.170 --> 00:11:09.140
I don’t want to show her
such an unsightly scene.

00:11:09.150 --> 00:11:10.850
Try and understand.

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:11.820
Yes, sir!

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:17.100
Does anyone know what time it is?

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:20.520
Sometime just after midnight.

00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:23.230
There’s no way dawn won’t come, is there?

00:11:23.230 --> 00:11:25.400
That’s just not possible!

00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:37.210
What’s the matter?

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:38.180
A noise.

00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:39.240
Oh, no!

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:41.810
It might be a visitor!

00:11:41.810 --> 00:11:43.010
Wait.

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:44.080
What is it?

00:11:44.080 --> 00:11:47.020
It’s impossible for anyone to visit.

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:48.720
How can you be so sure?

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:52.120
We’re surrounded by a barrier.

00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:55.150
The Mononoke’s territory
lies just outside that barrier.

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:03.690
It’s not possible for a human
to cross its territory for a visit.

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:04.960
Mononoke…

00:12:53.380 --> 00:12:55.200
Is it a cat?

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:49.670
Damn it!

00:13:49.670 --> 00:13:51.840
Why did this have to happen?

00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:54.090
Just as things were looking better.

00:13:54.090 --> 00:13:55.510
Damn it…

00:13:55.510 --> 00:13:56.600
Damn it!

00:14:15.570 --> 00:14:16.620
My dear…

00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:22.120
Mizue…

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:24.790
Mizue… Mizue…

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:28.460
Mizue… Mizue…

00:14:28.460 --> 00:14:29.570
Mizue?

00:14:33.050 --> 00:14:34.380
Mao…

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:37.550
Mao…

00:14:40.090 --> 00:14:42.890
Mao, I’m sorry…

00:14:42.890 --> 00:14:43.880
Mao!

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:48.090
My poor Mao!

00:15:16.860 --> 00:15:22.460
Lady Mi… zu… e…

00:15:32.540 --> 00:15:35.630
It’s Tamaki!

00:15:34.150 --> 00:15:35.610
Mizue?!

00:15:36.490 --> 00:15:38.200
Forgive me!

00:15:36.490 --> 00:15:38.200
Mizue?!

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:39.450
Tamaki?

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:40.880
Did she say Tamaki?!

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:43.190
Lady Mizue!

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:45.700
I’ll do anything to make it up to you!

00:15:45.720 --> 00:15:48.190
Stay away from me!

00:15:48.190 --> 00:15:49.680
Spare me!

00:15:52.500 --> 00:15:53.590
Oh, no!

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:56.390
What?!

00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:10.480
Get back!

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:13.110
Run to the back!

00:16:14.590 --> 00:16:15.980
Master Odajima!

00:16:28.450 --> 00:16:30.500
Mi… zue?

00:17:07.400 --> 00:17:09.340
You demon!

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:10.500
No!

00:17:14.580 --> 00:17:16.040
Ghost Cat!

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:20.910
Take this!

00:17:32.020 --> 00:17:34.090
Take some salt!

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:50.180
What are you angry about?

00:17:50.180 --> 00:17:52.660
What’s your Regret?!

00:17:52.660 --> 00:17:54.220
And your Truth?!

00:17:54.220 --> 00:17:55.450
What is it?!

00:18:00.120 --> 00:18:02.790
So that was the Mononoke, a Ghost Cat?

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:04.060
Yes.

00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:05.460
Where is Yoshiaki?

00:18:05.460 --> 00:18:07.230
Is Katsuyama dead?

00:18:10.100 --> 00:18:11.160
Most likely.

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:15.210
That’s a pity.

00:18:15.210 --> 00:18:16.710
Don’t bear a grudge.

00:18:16.710 --> 00:18:18.510
And if you must, then hold it

00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:20.530
against the Ghost Cat.

00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:20.530
Ms. Sato…

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:23.450
Who was that?

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:25.240
That was one part of the Truth.

00:18:26.880 --> 00:18:29.320
And the Form of the Regret.

00:18:29.320 --> 00:18:31.880
The lady of the house
referred to her as Tamaki.

00:18:32.990 --> 00:18:36.260
Does anyone know who she is?

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:42.070
What was that?

00:18:42.070 --> 00:18:44.900
The barrier has been broken in one room.

00:18:44.900 --> 00:18:46.440
It will be here very soon.

00:18:46.440 --> 00:18:48.040
Can’t you unsheathe it yet?

00:18:48.040 --> 00:18:49.640
Hurry up and do it!

00:18:49.640 --> 00:18:51.410
You’ll have to ask it yourself.

00:18:51.410 --> 00:18:52.640
Then again…

00:18:52.640 --> 00:18:54.310
Even if I manage
to unsheathe the sword…

00:18:54.310 --> 00:18:57.180
…there is no guarantee I will
triumph over the Mononoke’s power.

00:18:57.180 --> 00:18:59.480
What?! But you said
this was the Sword of Exorcism!

00:19:02.850 --> 00:19:05.590
A sword is manipulated

00:19:05.590 --> 00:19:06.680
by humans.

00:19:09.450 --> 00:19:13.620
There are limits to even my abilities.

00:19:17.710 --> 00:19:20.460
We can still retreat to the rooms further back.

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:56.660
Wow…

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:56.660
What the..

00:19:58.310 --> 00:20:00.300
Why is there a wedding kimono?

00:20:03.850 --> 00:20:05.280
It’s useless!

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:07.450
Useless! Useless! Useless!

00:20:07.450 --> 00:20:10.050
There’s no way out of this!

00:20:10.050 --> 00:20:13.430
You know something, don’t you?

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:22.020
It’s all your fault.

00:20:22.690 --> 00:20:24.480
It’s all your fault!

00:20:22.690 --> 00:20:24.480
That’s the wedding kimono

00:20:24.480 --> 00:20:28.320
You summoned the demon!

00:20:24.480 --> 00:20:26.480
the demon was wearing!

00:21:01.610 --> 00:21:03.270
I get it now.

00:21:03.270 --> 00:21:06.400
The Truth of the Ghost Cat was you all along!

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:09.960
<b><i>To be continued</i></b>

